// KR-69: `ARCH_RISCV64` is spelled correctly and is a real architecture — and no target kama knows
// has it, so nothing ever compiles this declaration and nothing ever analyses it. SPEC used to allow
// exactly this as "stub code for a platform you do not support yet"; the allowance was lifted 2026-09-18,
// because a rule that cannot tell it from a typo buys silence in both cases. Declaring the target —
// which BUILDING for riscv needs anyway — lifts the error and brings the code into `kama check`'s
// cover; tests/compilefor_declared_target.d is that same gate with the target declared.
@compileFor(ARCH_RISCV64)
fn int32 riscvOnly() { return 3; }

fn int32 main() { return 0; }
